addSaveMethod -- register a method for serializing a type to MRDI format
************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        addSaveMethod T
        addSaveMethod(T, dataFunc)
        addSaveMethod(T, paramsFunc, dataFunc)
  * Inputs:
      * T, a *note type: (Macaulay2Doc)Type,, the Macaulay2 type to be
        serialized
      * dataFunc, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, a function that
        takes an object of type T and returns the data to be stored in the data
        field of the MRDI JSON
      * paramsFunc, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, a function that
        takes an object of type T and returns the parameter object (e.g., the
        coefficient ring of a polynomial ring), which will itself be serialized
        recursively
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * UseID => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, if true, objects of this type are assigned UUIDs so they can be
        referenced rather than duplicated
      * Name => a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, default value
        FunctionClosure[../../../../../Macaulay2/m2/classes.m2:113:45-113:55],
        a function (or string) that determines the type name string for the
        _type field.  By default, the *note class: (Macaulay2Doc)class, of each
        object (as a string) is used.
      * Namespace => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        "Macaulay2", the namespace to register this save method under

Description
===========

This function registers a serialization method for the given type so that *note
saveMRDI: saveMRDI, knows how to convert objects of that type into MRDI JSON
format.

The zero-argument form addSaveMethod T is for types with no data and no
parameters (the MRDI output will contain only a _type field).

The one-argument form addSaveMethod(T, dataFunc) is for basic (non-parametric)
types whose MRDI representation needs only a _type name and data.  The dataFunc
receives the object and should return the data portion.

The two-argument form addSaveMethod(T, paramsFunc, dataFunc) is for parametric
types.  The paramsFunc returns an object representing the type's parameter
(which will be recursively serialized into the _type.params field), and
dataFunc returns the data.

The *note UseID: addSaveMethod, option causes objects of this type to be
assigned RFC 9562 version 4 UUIDs upon serialization. This is important for
types like polynomial rings that may be shared by many objects: the ring is
stored once in the _refs section and referenced by UUID elsewhere.

The *note Namespace: Namespace, option allows registering save methods for
different namespaces.  This is how OSCAR serialization support is implemented
alongside Macaulay2's own namespace.

Here we register a save method for a custom namespace.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : addNamespace("MySystem", "https://example.com", "1.0")                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : addSaveMethod(ZZ, identity, Name => "MyInt", Namespace => "MySystem")  |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : saveMRDI(42, Namespace => "MySystem")                                  |
|                                                                            |
|o3 = {"_ns": {"MySystem": ["https://example.com", "1.0"]}, "_type": "MyInt",|
|     "data": "42"}                                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note saveMRDI: saveMRDI, -- serialize a Macaulay2 object to MRDI JSON
    format

Ways to use addSaveMethod:
==========================

  * "addSaveMethod(Type)"
  * "addSaveMethod(Type,Function)"
  * "addSaveMethod(Type,Function,Function)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note addSaveMethod: addSaveMethod, is a *note method function with
options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

