addLoadMethod -- register a method for deserializing a type from MRDI format
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        addLoadMethod(typeName, f)
  * Inputs:
      * typeName, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the type name as it appears in the _type field of
        the MRDI JSON, or a list of strings to add multiple load methods at the
        same time
      * f, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, a function (params, data)
        -> Thing that reconstructs the object
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Namespace => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        "Macaulay2", the namespace to register this method under

Description
===========

This method registers a deserialization method so that *note loadMRDI:
loadMRDI, knows how to reconstruct objects of a given type within a given
namespace.

The namespace allows the same file format to be used across different computer
algebra systems.  The Macaulay2 namespace is "Macaulay2" and the OSCAR
namespace is "Oscar".  Each namespace maintains its own type registry.  Use
*note addNamespace: addNamespace, to register a new namespace before adding
load methods to it.

The loading function f receives two arguments:

  * params: For parametric types (e.g., *note RingElement:
    (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,), this is the already-deserialized parameter
    (e.g., the parent ring).  For non-parametric types (e.g., *note ZZ:
    (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,), this is *note null: (Macaulay2Doc)null,.
  * data:  The contents of the data field from the JSON, recursively
    deserialized.

The *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, form allows registering the same function
for multiple type names at once, which is useful when systems use different
names for equivalent types.

Here we register a load method for a custom namespace.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : addNamespace("MySystem", "https://example.com", "1.0")                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : addLoadMethod("MyInt",                                                  |
|         (params, data) -> value data,                                       |
|         Namespace => "MySystem")                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = FunctionClosure[currentString:3:4-3:32]                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : FunctionClosure                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : loadMRDI "{\"_ns\":{\"MySystem\":[\"https://example.com\",\"1.0\"]},\"_ |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = 42                                                                      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|type\":\"MyInt\",\"data\":\"42\"}"                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note loadMRDI: loadMRDI, -- deserialize a Macaulay2 object from MRDI
    format

Ways to use addLoadMethod:
==========================

  * "addLoadMethod(List,Function)"
  * "addLoadMethod(String,Function)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note addLoadMethod: addLoadMethod, is a *note method function with
options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

