validateMRDI -- validate an MRDI JSON object against the format specification
*****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        validateMRDI s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or a *note hash table:
        (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, a JSON string or parsed JSON hash table to
        validate

Description
===========

Validates that a JSON string or hash table conforms to the MRDI file format
specification (see https://www.oscar-system.org/schemas/mrdi.json ). This
checks structural requirements such as:

  * the presence of a _type key
  * that _type is a string or an object with string-valued name
  * that _ns and _refs are objects (if present)
  * that all keys of _refs are valid UUIDs
  * that referenced objects are themselves valid MRDI

The function produces an error if validation fails and returns *note null:
(Macaulay2Doc)null, on success.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : s = saveMRDI 5                                                       |
|                                                                          |
|o1 = {"_ns": {"Macaulay2": ["https://macaulay2.com", "1.26.05"]}, "_type":|
|     "ZZ", "data": "5"}                                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : validateMRDI s                                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use validateMRDI:
=========================

  * "validateMRDI(HashTable)"
  * "validateMRDI(String)"
  * "validateMRDI(Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note validateMRDI: validateMRDI, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

